   - As point P moves around the unit circle, a corresponding point on the graph of y = sin(x) will move horizontally from left to right, tracing out the sine wave in synchronization with the movement of P.
   - The horizontal position of the point on the sine wave graph will be determined by the angle of point P from the positive x-axis, with 0 radians corresponding to the leftmost point of the graph and increasing angles moving to the right.

